WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.310
In a multiple-choice question,

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.750
the options are information.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.510
You can test them, or rule some out,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.390
without solving the whole problem.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.660
But an option that merely looks familiar

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.790
is not evidence.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.080
Every choice still has to be checked

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.130
against the question.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.580
Question setters include options that match common

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.790
mistakes, and options that match a step along the way.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.160
Using the options well, and rereading what was asked,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.430
protects you from both.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.860
Which of these numbers is a multiple of both four and

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.930
nine: fifty-four, sixty-four, seventy-two,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.530
eighty-one or ninety?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.920
Pause and think about the quickest way to

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.910
rule options out.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.720
A multiple of four is even, so eighty-one goes.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.320
Half of fifty-four is twenty-seven, which is odd,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.140
so fifty-four is not a multiple of four.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:52.860
The same happens with ninety.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.420
That leaves sixty-four and seventy-two.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.100
For nine, add the digits.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.840
Sixty-four gives ten, so it is not a multiple of nine.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.540
Seventy-two gives nine, so it is.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.520
The answer is seventy-two, option C.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.320
Two quick tests replaced any long division.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.480
Now the other trap.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.350
A book costs twelve dollars and a pen costs

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.420
three dollars less.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.360
What do two pens cost?

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.670
One pen costs nine dollars, and nine is

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.460
among the options.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.860
But the question asks for two pens: eighteen.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:29.010
Always reread the request before choosing.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.680
When an equation is hard to solve directly,

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.360
try the options in it.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:37.160
Suppose two times x plus five must be nineteen.

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.940
Try six: the result is seventeen.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.120
Here bigger choices give bigger results, so try seven.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.120
That gives nineteen.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.870
Check how the expression changes before using a trial to

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:49.620
choose a direction.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.540
Rule options out with quick tests.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.290
Do not choose a number just because it appeared

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.200
in your working.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.660
Reread what was asked before you answer.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.960
Notebook challenge: which of forty-five, sixty,

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.870
seventy-five and ninety is a multiple of both

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:05.840
four and five?
